Read the complete account of pressure realization, gauge principles, comparison calibration and quadrupole analysis. Derive how a gas-dependent signal is turned into a reported pressure and examine what information is lost in an unknown mixture. Compare a reference calibration with the conditions at the actual gauge port.

Metadata and selected gauge-principle, ionization-sensitivity, comparison-calibration, quadrupole-source/filter and detection passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The rod geometry and equations on PDF page 8 were checked visually. The learning Record derives its own explicit SI potential/voltage convention rather than copying unexplained numerical coefficients. The paper explains that comparison requires matching molecular density and velocity distributions, a stronger condition than matching a scalar pressure reading. Standards references describe the paper's period; consult the actual current edition when a specific standards claim is required.

